4. SHARED APP LINK MUST NEVER GRANT OWNER
   OR ADMINISTRATOR PERMISSIONS
==================================================

Fix authorization issues associated with sharing the application's URL.

Requirements:
- Anyone opening the shared application link must initially receive only the permissions appropriate to their authenticated identity or guest session.
- Sharing the app link must never grant owner or administrator privileges.
- Do not use URL parameters, query strings, browser storage, client-side flags, or frontend conditions as the source of administrative authorization.
- Do not grant administrator privileges based on a shared link, deployment URL, Google Cloud URL, or possession of a particular route.
- Opening an administrator dashboard URL must not grant access to the dashboard.
- Protect administrator pages and APIs using server-side authorization checks.
- Verify the authenticated user's role before allowing access to sensitive resources.
- Return an appropriate unauthorized or forbidden response when a normal user or guest attempts to access restricted resources.
- Do not expose owner-only information in publicly accessible application responses.

The same security rules must apply regardless of how a person opens the application.

