6. MULTIPLE-DEVICE LOGIN SUPPORT
==================================================

Allow the owner, administrators, and normal users to use the application on multiple devices simultaneously.

Requirements:
- Support simultaneous sessions on devices such as laptops, desktop computers, tablets, and mobile phones.
- Do not automatically log out an existing session merely because the same user signs in on another device, unless a documented security policy requires it.
- Ensure the same account's preferred name, account identity, and permissions remain consistent across devices.
- Keep authentication sessions independent and secure.
- Track each session separately.
- Allow expired or revoked sessions to be invalidated appropriately.
- Ensure logging out on one device follows the application's documented logout policy.
- Provide a secure way to terminate individual sessions or revoke sessions where appropriate.
- Never share authentication tokens or session credentials between different users.
- Do not rely solely on local storage to identify a user or determine their role.
- Protect against session fixation, token leakage, and unauthorized session reuse.

The owner and administrators must be able to access the application from multiple devices without accidentally changing their roles or losing their permissions.

